\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Heavenly Father, Thou hast brought us
\par Safely to the present day,
\par Gently leading on our footsteps,
\par Watching o'er us all the way,
\par Friend and Guide through life's long journey,
\par Grateful hearts to Thee we bring;
\par But for love so true and challengeless
\par How shall we fit praises sing?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Mercies new and never-falling
\par Brightly shine through all the past
\par Watchful care and loving-kindness
\par Always near from first to last,
\par Tender love, divine protection 
\par Ever with us day and night;
\par Blessings more than we can number
\par Strow the path with golden light.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Shadows deep have crossed our pathway;
\par We have trembled in the storm;
\par Clouds have gathered round so darkly
\par That we could not see Thy form;
\par Yet Thy love hath never left us
\par In our griefs alone to be,
\par And the help each gave the other
\par Was the strength that came from Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Many that we loved have left us,
\par Reaching first their journey's end;
\par Now they wait to give us welcome,
\par Brother, sister, child, and friend,
\par When at last our journey's over,
\par And we pass away from sight,
\par Father, take us through the darkness
\par Into everlasting light.
\par Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

